.TH MKISO 1 "2026-08-31" "SPS 1.0" "SPS Commands"
.SH NAME
mkiso \- build an SPS Linux live ISO (Splux)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
mkiso --output FILE.iso [options]
mkiso --layout DIR [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkiso
builds a hybrid ISO for
.B SPS Linux
(informally Splux). The image boots with a real init as PID 1 and
.BR setup (1)
on PATH. Default
.B --init
is systemd. If the build host has no systemd binaries, busybox init
respawns gettys on tty1 and ttyS0 instead of exec-ing a shell as PID 1.
SPS the package system does not require these images.
.PP
Flash it to USB, boot, and run
.B setup .
.B --session plasma
copies a host Plasma/Wayland stack; NVIDIA live graphics use nouveau.
.B --layout
writes the live root only, for tests and inspection.
.PP
Host compiler tools can be copied into the image so
.B setup
can build packages from the bundled recipes. Pass
.B --no-seed
to omit them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --output " file"
Write a bootable ISO.
.TP
.BI --layout " dir"
Populate a live root and exit.
.TP
.BI --session " name"
.B tty
or
.B plasma .
.TP
.BI --init " name"
.B systemd
or
.B openrc .
Default systemd.
.TP
.BI --busybox " file"
Static busybox used for the initramfs and live
.BR /bin/busybox .
.TP
.BI --kernel " file"
Live kernel. Defaults to
.IR /boot/vmlinuz .
.TP
.BI --core " dir"
.TP
.BI --extra " dir"
Copy recipe trees to
.I /usr/src/sps/core
and
.IR /usr/src/sps/extra .
.TP
.B --with-rust
.TP
.B --with-go
Copy those host toolchains into the live image.
.TP
.B --with-firmware
Copy
.I /lib/firmware
into the squashfs. This tree is often more than a gigabyte, so published
ISOs omit it. Wireless adapters that need blobs will need firmware copied
onto the target after install, or a locally built image with this flag.
.TP
.B --no-modules
Do not copy the full
.I /lib/modules
tree into the squashfs. The initramfs still gets squashfs/overlay/USB
modules so the disc can boot.
.TP
.B --no-seed
Do not copy gcc, Python, and related host tools.
.SH FILES
.I $SPS_LIBDIR/mkiso
holds the live init scripts, motd, and seed binary list.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setup (1),
.BR sget (1),
.BR src (1)
